  "question": {
    "text": "Three positive numbers form an increasing <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the middle term in this <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo></math> is doubled, the new numbers are in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Then the common ratio of the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo></math> is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
